' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---
' The consumer side: the formatter reads the convention cache, and the
' registrar warms the cache and keeps it current.
ores::refdata::client::presentation::currency_pair_rate_formatter ..> ores::refdata::service::cache::currency_pair_convention_cache : reads conventions

note as N_CLI_WARM
  The warm path is the canonical list paged to its end: the protocol has no
  bulk read, so load() walks offset/limit until a response reports none left,
  and the registrar subscribes the changed events on top of it.
end note
ores::refdata::service::cache::currency_pair_convention_cache .. N_CLI_WARM


